COPY public.platforms (id, name, description, status, image, display_order, created_at, updated_at) FROM stdin;
6	SEEDS AND NURSERIES	Seeds and nurseries are the first and most important stage of the wood value chain. They ensure the availability of strong, healthy tree seedlings for sustainable forestry and future wood production.	published	uploads/platforms/platform_1763040985.jpg	0	2025-10-08 18:49:52+00	2025-11-24 11:45:35+00
7	Primary wood processing	Primary wood processing is the first stage of transforming raw logs into usable wood materials. At this level, timber is converted into boards, planks, beams, and other basic wood products that feed into the rest of the value chain.	published	uploads/platforms/platform_1763981607.JPG	0	2025-11-24 10:53:27+00	2025-11-24 11:47:53+00
8	secondary wood processing	Secondary wood processing is the stage where processed timber is transformed into finished or semi-finished products. This is where value addition happens, turning basic timber into furniture, building materials, and other high-quality wood products.	published	uploads/platforms/platform_1763985127.jpg	0	2025-11-24 11:51:47+00	2025-11-24 11:52:07+00
9	Tertiary wood Processing	Tertiary wood processing is the stage where finished wooden products are designed, assembled, customized, and prepared for end-users. It focuses on producing ready-to-use items that go directly to consumers, businesses, or markets.	published	uploads/platforms/platform_1764007114.jpg	0	2025-11-24 17:46:19+00	2025-11-24 17:58:34+00
10	Sales and Distribution	Sales and distribution involve bringing finished wooden products to the market, connecting producers with customers, retailers, wholesalers, and export opportunities. It ensures that wood products reach buyers efficiently and profitably.	published	uploads/platforms/platform_1764006533.jpg	0	2025-11-24 17:48:32+00	2025-11-24 17:48:53+00
11	Forest management	Forest management involves planting, protecting, and sustainably using forests to ensure a continuous supply of timber while preserving the environment for future generations.	published	uploads/platforms/platform_1764007455.jpg	0	2025-11-24 18:04:15+00	2025-11-24 18:04:15+00
\.
